// breathes, and the water carries its top over), to its rounded tip. Each substep:\r
// 1. reefPredict (every node but the roots): the water carries it (an implicit drag, weaker along\r
//    the tentacle than across it, towards the flow it feels: the simulated flow averaged over\r
//    the last moments, rFlow, for a finger of soft tissue full of water has weight, it sways\r
//    after the water, smoothly, never flicking with every stir; and of the water's motion past\r
//    the anemone, which the globe carries round, only part, up to a speed it keeps up with: the\r
//    water slips past a finger held at its root, in faster water it leans out with the flow\r
//    rather than flying about); out of the water it hangs, limp. The predicted position goes to\r
//    rPred. (Its own velocity is only ever the water's, its pushes and pulls: a slow drag would\r
//    keep every shove from a fish or its neighbours going, and the fingers would wander.)\r
// 2. reefTentacles (every tentacle, root to tip): the root where the disc holds it. Each node is\r
//    held at its link's length from the one before, towards its prediction (follow-the-leader,\r
//    an exactly inextensible rope in one pass), and kept out of the clownfish, the anemone's own\r
