//    dynamic FTL correction, Müller et al. 2012; the pushes kept out of the correction). Then\r
//    the tentacle takes back the shape it holds (each link eased towards its rest turn from the\r
//    link before it; the first link, the way it grows from the disc), as positions only: in the\r
//    water that pull is slow and overdamped, it never swings past the shape.\r
